dodo-session (0.5.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Desktops are added and removed by the user, as on macOS, and stay while
    empty: Super+= adds one, Super+- removes the current one, Super+Right on
    the last desktop adds one unless it is empty. Super+Shift+Left/Right
    take the window along (labwc AddDesktop and RemoveDesktop, Dodobian
    patch 0004). The mouse wheel on the desktop only leafs through the
    desktops there are.
  * Super+F maximizes the window and restores it, as Super+Up will open the
    desktop overview.
  * Desktops slide sideways in half a second and a pill of dots shows which
    one you are on (labwc slideTime and popupStyle, Dodobian patch 0005).
  * Every desktop of a monitor shows the monitor's wallpaper: a desktop added
    later was black, as xfdesktop only had wallpapers for desktops 1 to 4.

 -- dmitrax <4255553+dmitrax@users.noreply.github.com>  Fri, 27 Nov 2026 21:00:00 +0400

dodo-session (0.4.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Every monitor has desktops of its own, created as needed and named by
    position (labwc <desktops perOutput dynamic>, Dodobian patch 0004).
  * The pinned= monitor of session.conf is gone with its login-time labwc
    layer and the split panel: a monitor keeps its desktop while another one
    switches. An old pinned= key is ignored, and the log says so.

 -- dmitrax <4255553+dmitrax@users.noreply.github.com>  Fri, 27 Nov 2026 20:00:00 +0400

